WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.960
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:04.900
LARRY ARNN: This is a joining
of USA Shooting and Hillsdale

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.130
College.

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:08.570
The word college
means partnership.

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:10.480
Partnerships always
flourish when

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.760
they serve a common purpose.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.790
Hillsdale College was founded
to pursue four things that

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:17.350
form an integrity--

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:21.510
high learning, character,
freedom, and faith.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.670
JAY WALDRON: The partnership
with Hillsdale and USA Shooting

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.570
is super exciting.

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:29.350
It's going to be a very
powerful thing for us,

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:34.880
just having a great partner with
like values, like Hillsdale.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.130
KIM RHODE: Shooting was
something that was passed down

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.110
generationally in my family.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:40.580
And it teaches you
a lot of things

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:43.850
that you use in life every
day, like responsibility,

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:45.330
discipline, focus.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:49.490
And that's really where you
see meld between Hillsdale

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:52.310
and USA Shooting come
together to really teach that

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:55.787
to the youth, to kids,
and to future generations.

00:00:55.787 --> 00:00:57.620
These are things that
they'll take with them

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:58.873
for the rest of their lives.

00:00:58.873 --> 00:01:00.290
And at the end of
the day, they're

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:04.069
creating a legacy, not
just for the school,

00:01:04.069 --> 00:01:08.215
but also for the future
of the shooting sports.

00:01:08.215 --> 00:01:09.840
BART SPIETH: Working
with USA Shooting,

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.010
we have the opportunity
to introduce more youth

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:16.910
to shooting sports than has
ever happened at any college.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:20.320
And we have an ability to
do that at a high level.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.360
JAY WALDRON: USA Shooting
brings in the Olympic

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:25.330
Ring, which is a pretty
powerful statement in itself.

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:28.648
It's the best of the best,
the most elite athletes.

00:01:28.648 --> 00:01:30.940
BART SPIETH: Being able to
work with youth to give them

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:35.020
that opportunity to
pursue an Olympic path

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:38.260
is a unique thing for a
school and a great thing

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:39.730
for Hillsdale College.

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:43.600
And we hope to see some
Olympic athletes coming out

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:47.170
of Hillsdale College, right
through the Halter Center.

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:50.500
RICH PEWE: For 175
years, Hillsdale College

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:53.110
has been providing the
type of education that

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:55.030
makes possible for [INAUDIBLE].

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:58.540
And one of the pillars of
that education is character.

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:02.230
One of the ways to develop
character, at an early age,

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:04.200
is through shooting sports.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.850
LARRY ARNN:
Hillsdale College, it

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:10.560
has been an academic,
informed voice

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.302
to keep the Declaration
of Independence

00:02:12.302 --> 00:02:14.010
and the Constitution
of the United States

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:18.310
in their sovereign place
because it's in our bones.

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:20.400
The Olympics are great.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.350
Shooting is important.

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:25.470
It should be cultivated,
and the responsibility

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.040
that goes with it.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.950
There's our partnership.

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:30.060
We are proud of it.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:33.410
[MUSIC PLAYING]

